.TH TOUCHCUE 1
.SH NAME
touchcue \- Shows who is waiting for your security key touch
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtouchcue\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows who is waiting for your security key touch
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Configuration file [default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/touchcue/config.toml]
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Log more: \-v for info, \-vv for debug; TOUCHCUE_LOG overrides it
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBrun\fR
Run the daemon in the foreground
.TP
\fBcheck\fR
Check the configuration, desktop capabilities and devices
.TP
\fBlist\-devices\fR
List the connected FIDO devices
.TP
\fBtrace\fR
Print touch detection signals until interrupted
.TP
\fBgpg\fR
Set up touch detection for gpg and ssh through gpg\-agent
.TP
\fBgpg install\fR
Make gpg\-agent run touchcue as its scdaemon
.TP
\fBgpg uninstall\fR
Stop gpg\-agent from running touchcue as its scdaemon
.TP
\fBaskpass\fR
Answer an OpenSSH askpass prompt
.SH "TOUCHCUE RUN"
Run the daemon in the foreground
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR touchcue run [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "TOUCHCUE CHECK"
Check the configuration, desktop capabilities and devices
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR touchcue check [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "TOUCHCUE LIST-DEVICES"
List the connected FIDO devices
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR touchcue list\-devices [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "TOUCHCUE TRACE"
Print touch detection signals until interrupted
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR touchcue trace [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "TOUCHCUE GPG"
Set up touch detection for gpg and ssh through gpg\-agent
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR touchcue gpg [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "TOUCHCUE GPG INSTALL"
Make gpg\-agent run touchcue as its scdaemon
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR touchcue gpg install [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "TOUCHCUE GPG UNINSTALL"
Stop gpg\-agent from running touchcue as its scdaemon
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR touchcue gpg uninstall [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\-backup\fR
Replace gpg\-agent.conf with the backup taken by install, then delete the backup
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "TOUCHCUE ASKPASS"
Answer an OpenSSH askpass prompt

OpenSSH runs the `SSH_ASKPASS` program with no extra arguments, so point it at a link to touchcue named `touchcue\-askpass`. `touchcue askpass` passes every argument after it through unparsed.
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR touchcue askpass [OPTIONS] [<MESSAGE>] ...
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<MESSAGE>\fR
The prompt OpenSSH passes
